 "lines": [
  {
   "scene": 1,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "In 1947, a moth made a computer fail.",
   "start": 0.15,
   "end": 3.222
  },
  {
   "scene": 2,
   "speaker": "leo",
   "text": "Wait. A moth? Like… you?",
   "start": 3.672,
   "end": 5.421
  },
  {
   "scene": 3,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "Like me. Picture Harvard, 1947. The Mark II.",
   "start": 5.871,
   "end": 9.306
  },
  {
   "scene": 4,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "A room full of relays: little metal switches that click open and shut to do math.",
   "start": 9.756,
   "end": 14.321
  },
  {
   "scene": 5,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "On September 9th, it started making errors. So the team went looking for the problem…",
   "start": 14.771,
   "end": 19.742
  },
  {
   "scene": 6,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "and found her. A moth, stuck between the contacts.",
   "start": 20.192,
   "end": 22.816
  },
  {
   "scene": 7,
   "speaker": "leo",
   "text": "No way.",
   "start": 23.266,
   "end": 24.183
  },
  {
   "scene": 8,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "So they did the most engineer thing ever. They taped her into the logbook, and wrote:",
   "start": 24.633,
   "end": 29.071
  },
  {
   "scene": 9,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "\"First actual case of bug being found.\"",
   "start": 29.521,
   "end": 31.761
  },
  {
   "scene": 10,
   "speaker": "leo",
   "text": "So that's where \"bug\" comes from!",
   "start": 32.211,
   "end": 33.96
  },
  {
   "scene": 11,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "Nope. Engineers already called glitches bugs. Edison wrote it in 1878.",
   "start": 34.41,
   "end": 39.658
  },
  {
   "scene": 12,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "That's the joke. An actual bug.",
   "start": 40.108,
   "end": 41.793
  },
  {
   "scene": 13,
   "speaker": "leo",
   "text": "And Grace Hopper found it, right?",
   "start": 42.243,
   "end": 44.163
  },
  {
   "scene": 14,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "Bright light. Lamp or fire? She was on the team, and she helped make the story famous.",
   "start": 44.613,
   "end": 49.264
  },
  {
   "scene": 15,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "That page is still kept at the Smithsonian. Moth included.",
   "start": 49.714,
   "end": 53.149
  },
  {
   "scene": 16,
   "speaker": "leo",
   "text": "So every time I debug something…",
   "start": 53.599,
   "end": 55.775
  },
  {
   "scene": 17,
   "speaker": "mott",
   "text": "…you're talking about my family. Stay curious. Not too close to the light.",
   "start": 56.225,
   "end": 60.235
  }
 ],
